{
  "name": "model-hub-det (settings Model Hub, operator + builder, seeded 2 installed models, guarded delete to boundary, selectOption filters, gibberish empty state, download button to boundary only)",
  "stopOnError": false,
  "notes": [
    "model-results-clear-filters is played through the invoke stub: search_hf_models (lib/ipc/modelHub.ts:133-134) is answered with three gated cards, model-filter-gated is set to open so filteredResults empties while searchResults keeps its 3 (ModelHub.svelte:87-100), which is the only way the no-match branch renders (ModelResults.svelte:99-108); the click runs clearFilters (ModelHub.svelte:255-260) and the three cards come back. The resolve imitates the SearchPage / HfModelCard types (apollia-llm hf_registry.rs:56-81), so it drifts if they change.",
    "model-load-more is played through the same stub: a once stub answers page 1 with next_cursor automation-page-2 so hasMore is true (ModelHub.svelte:165-167), the standing stub answers the load-more call with one card and a null cursor, so the button disappears and a third model-card- renders. The block sits after the live gibberish search, not before it: search() assigns searchResults only on success (ModelHub.svelte:165-169), so once the stub has put three cards on screen an offline or refused live search leaves them there and model-results-empty (ModelResults.svelte:74, results.length must be 0) can no longer render. The builder pass that follows remounts the route, which resets the stubbed results."
  ],
